.TH POL 8 "2026-11-09" "nni @VERSION@" "nni family manual"
.SH NAME
pol \- Package Optimized Layer, the YnniOS package manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pol
.I COMMAND
.RI [ PACKAGE ...]
.RI [ "apt options" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pol
is how packages are installed on YnniOS. It drives Debian's apt
underneath; the apt, apt\-get and apt\-cache commands are moved to
.I /usr/lib/pol/
on purpose so that
.B pol
is the one tool to use. Package names are Debian package names.
Recommended packages are not installed, to keep the system small.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Refresh the package lists. Run it first after booting.
.TP
.B upgrade
Upgrade installed packages.
.TP
.B full\-upgrade
Upgrade, allowing packages to be added or removed.
.TP
.BI install " PACKAGE..."
Install packages.
.TP
.BI reinstall " PACKAGE..."
Reinstall packages (puts deleted files back).
.TP
.BI remove " PACKAGE..."
Remove packages.
.TP
.BI purge " PACKAGE..."
Remove packages and their configuration.
.TP
.B autoremove
Remove packages nothing needs any more.
.TP
.B clean
Empty the download cache.
.TP
.BI search " TERM"
Search the package lists.
.TP
.BI show " PACKAGE"
Package details.
.TP
.BI policy " PACKAGE"
Available versions and where they come from.
.TP
.B list
Installed packages.
.TP
.BI files " PACKAGE"
Files a package installed.
.TP
.BI owns " FILE"
Which package a file belongs to.
.PP
Options such as
.B \-y
are passed on to apt.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list ", " /etc/apt/sources.list.d/
Package sources, including the nni repository (nni.sources).
.TP
.I /usr/lib/pol/
The real apt tools.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
pol update
pol search editor
pol install nano
pol owns /usr/bin/fastfetch
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR spol (8),
.BR nni (8),
.BR apt\-get (8)
